<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Real life: average and instantaneous rate of change of area or volume (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The {@shapew@} of radius \( r \) cm is</p>
\[ {@fsym@}(r) = {@fr@}. \]
<p>Give exact answers in terms of \( \pi \) (type <code>pi</code>).</p>
<p>(a) Find the <strong>average</strong> rate of change of \( {@fsym@} \) as \( r \) increases from \( {@r1@} \) cm to \( {@r2@} \) cm.</p>
<div>Average rate \( = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) Find \( {@fsym@}'(r) \).</p>
<div>\( {@fsym@}'(r) = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p>(c) Find the <strong>instantaneous</strong> rate of change of \( {@fsym@} \) when \( r = {@r0@} \) cm.</p>
<div>\( {@fsym@}'({@r0@}) = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>
<p>(d) What are the units of your answer to (c)?</p>
<div>[[input:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> The average rate of change is the gradient of the chord:</p>
\[ \frac{ {@fsym@}({@r2@}) - {@fsym@}({@r1@}) }{ {@r2@} - {@r1@} } = \frac{ {@f2@} - {@f1@} }{ {@r2 - r1@} } = {@ta1@}. \]
<p><strong>(b)</strong> By the power rule (the constant \( {@kc@} \) is just a multiplier), \( {@fsym@}'(r) = {@dfr@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(c)</strong> \( {@fsym@}'({@r0@}) = {@ta3@} \approx {@float(ta3)@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(d)</strong> \( {@fsym@} \) is measured in {@outu@} and \( r \) in cm, so the rate is in <strong>{@outu@} per cm</strong>: {@outu@} of extra {@qw@} for each extra centimetre of radius.</p>
<p>The average rate in (a) describes the whole interval from \( {@r1@} \) to \( {@r2@} \) cm; the derivative in (c) describes the single instant \( r = {@r0@} \) cm.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025010100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[/* Circle area or sphere volume, chosen at random. */
sh : rand(2);
kc : if sh = 0 then %pi else 4*%pi/3;
nn : if sh = 0 then 2 else 3;
fr : kc*r^nn;
fsym : if sh = 0 then A else V;
shapew : if sh = 0 then "area (in cm²) of a circle" else "volume (in cm³) of a sphere";
outu : if sh = 0 then "cm²" else "cm³";
qw : if sh = 0 then "area" else "volume";
dfr : diff(fr, r);
r1 : rand([1, 2, 3]);
r2 : r1 + rand([2, 3]);
/* Exclude r0 = nn: there f(r0) = f'(r0) (e.g. A(2) = A'(2) = 4 pi), which would
   hide the "gave the value, not the rate" mistake. */
r0 : rand_with_prohib(2, 6, [r1, r2, nn]);
f1 : subst(r1, r, fr);
f2 : subst(r2, r, fr);
ta1 : (f2 - f1)/(r2 - r1);                  /* average rate */
ta3 : subst(r0, r, dfr);                     /* instantaneous rate */
w_nodiv : f2 - f1;                           /* forgot to divide by the change in r */
w_f0 : subst(r0, r, fr);                     /* gave the area/volume, not its rate */
w_nomult : kc*r^(nn - 1);                    /* lowered the power without multiplying */
opts4 : random_permutation([
  [1, true,  sconcat(outu, " per cm")],
  [2, false, outu],
  [3, false, "cm"],
  [4, false, sconcat("cm per ", outu)]]);]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
